INFOSEC-News
Collect cybersecurity news published in the last 24 hours and share articles that mention CVEs rated High or Critical by NVD (CVSS 7.0 or higher).

Setup
Requires Python 3.10 or newer.

python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt

Run a preview (the default; this does not send anything):

python infosec_news.py

The default RSS sources are SecurityWeek, Dark Reading, The Hacker News, and CISA Cybersecurity Advisories. Set NEWS_FEEDS to a comma-separated list of feed URLs to replace them. Use --hours 12 to change the lookback window.

Sharing
Configure one or both delivery methods with environment variables. Email can target multiple recipients or a distribution list. A Slack incoming webhook can post to a channel (or a group that includes that channel).

Email settings:

SMTP_HOST (required to enable email)
SMTP_PORT (default: 587; port 465 uses implicit TLS)
SMTP_USER and SMTP_PASSWORD (optional if the SMTP server does not require authentication)
EMAIL_FROM (defaults to SMTP_USER)
EMAIL_TO (comma-separated addresses)
Slack setting:

SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL
To deliver the report, pass --send:

python infosec_news.py --send

The collector only shares entries that include a CVE identifier with an NVD CVSS base score of at least 7.0. Articles without a matching score are omitted, not assigned a severity based on wording. NVD lookups require internet access; set NVD_API_KEY to use an API key and raise the public rate limit. The script does not schedule itself; run it from cron or another scheduler for recurring digests. Review a preview before enabling scheduled delivery.
